meta {
  name: Print All Order Reports
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/lab-reports/order/{{orderId}}/print-all
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "templateId": "{{pdfReportTemplateId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Render ALL of an order's reports into one consolidated PDF, streamed back as
  `application/pdf`. Two render paths, chosen by the resolved template's `type`:

  ## Render paths
  - **`lab_all_report` / `patient_lab_all_report` template** → the whole order is
    ONE continuous Latte document. The context is
    `{ report_tests: { groups: [], tests: [...] }, header_fields: {...} }`, where
    each `report_tests.tests[]` entry carries a **`body_html`** field — the
    **Body HTML** tag. Crucially, each test's `body_html` is that test's OWN
    fully-rendered single-report `lab_report` template body (resolved per test via
    Test-Template → Configuration default → first-active, exactly like a
    standalone print), so every test preserves its complete designed report
    structure. The template iterates them one after another, e.g.:

    ```latte
    {foreach $report_tests->tests as $report}
      {$report->body_html|noescape}
    {/foreach}
    ```

    Only the single-report template's BODY is rendered per test (not its header),
    so the patient/order header is not duplicated — the shared header comes from
    the all-report template's own header block + `{$header_fields->...}`. This
    mirrors the legacy ezHealthTrack "Body HTML" behaviour. When a test has no
    single-report template configured, its `body_html` falls back to a built-in
    minimal results table so the combined PDF still renders.

  - **`lab_report` template (or none)** → each report is rendered as its own
    complete single-report PDF and the pages are merged with `pdf-lib`.

  ## Body
  - `templateId` (optional) — the template to render with. Supply a
    `lab_all_report` template id for the Body-HTML loop path above; omit to fall
    back to per-report resolution + merge.
  - `orderItemIds` (optional) — array of `OrderItem` UUIDs. When given (non-empty),
    only the reports belonging to these order items are included in the
    consolidated PDF instead of every report on the order. Used by the Order
    Overview modal's multi-select "Download Report" / "Print All Report" bulk
    actions, which must only act on the technician's selected rows. Omit for the
    unfiltered whole-order render (unchanged default behaviour).

  ## Related
  - `POST /lab-reports/:id/print` renders a SINGLE report. Its body now also
    accepts an optional `type` (`lab_report` | `lab_panel`, default `lab_report`),
    used only to resolve the default template when no `templateId` is given — the
    same report record renders either way. The `lab_all_report` path reuses this
    exact single-report resolution + body rendering to build each test's
    `body_html`.

  ## Errors
  - 404 `LAB_REPORT_NOT_FOUND` — the order (or the selected `orderItemIds`) has no
    reports.
  - 404 `NO_ACTIVE_PRINT_TEMPLATE` / 409 `AMBIGUOUS_PRINT_TEMPLATE` — template
    resolution failed and no `templateId` was supplied.

  In Bruno, use "Save Response → Save to file" to inspect the PDF.
}
